# ---- codesec auth ----
#
# codesec inherits upstream audit's auth modes. Pick ONE block below.
# Then run `codesec auth-check` to confirm.

# (a) Claude subscription OAuth (headless, CI): generate with `claude setup-token`.
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY MUST be unset or it silently routes to metered billing.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# (b) Claude metered API key (opt in with --allow-api-key / CODESEC_ALLOW_API_KEY=1):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# (c) Generic Anthropic-compatible gateway (OpenRouter, proxy, ...):
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...

# ============================================================
# Provider presets (preferred way to use z.ai / Unsloth).
# Set CODESEC_PROVIDER on the CLI or here, then the matching key.
# Run `codesec providers` to list presets.
# ============================================================

# --- Z.AI GLM Coding Plan (https://docs.z.ai/devpack/overview) ---
# Anthropic endpoint: https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic
# Get a key at https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list (requires a GLM Coding Plan).
# Codesec maps stages automatically: recon/validate/trace -> glm-5.2,
# hunt/gapfill/dedupe/feedback/report -> glm-4.7 (deliberate disagreement preserved).
# CODESEC_PROVIDER=zai
# ZAI_API_KEY=

# --- Unsloth Studio local server (https://unsloth.ai/docs/basics/api) ---
# Start Unsloth Studio, load a GGUF model, create an API key (sk-unsloth-...).
# Default port 8888; override with CODESEC_BASE_URL if different.
# One model is loaded at a time, so pass CODESEC_MODEL (exact id from
# GET http://localhost:8888/v1/models) — this collapses deliberate disagreement.
# CODESEC_PROVIDER=unsloth
# UNSLOTH_API_KEY=sk-unsloth-...
# CODESEC_MODEL=unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF
# CODESEC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8888

# Hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint (see config/hetzner.yaml):
# export HETZNER_API_KEY=...   # token from inference.hetzner.com console

# Optional: force a single model across every stage for any provider.
# CODESEC_MODEL=
